# How to cite this software. GitHub reads this file and offers a "Cite this
# repository" button from it; `cffconvert` turns it into BibTeX.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Onset-HFO: detecting high-frequency oscillations in intracranial EEG, with an evidence-only agent"
abstract: >-
  A research prototype for detecting high-frequency oscillations and interictal
  epileptiform discharges in intracranial EEG. It ships four HFO detectors, a
  spike detector, artifact validation, data-quality checks that remove only
  what no physiology produces, Poisson confidence intervals and a candidate
  channel set rather than a single argmax; an installable desktop reviewer
  built on MNE's own Qt browser; and an agent that answers only from the saved
  result tables and cites them. Evaluated against the expert HFO markings and
  the surgical outcomes of OpenNeuro ds003498. Not a medical device, and not
  validated for clinical use.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abibullaev
    given-names: Berdakh
    email: berdakho@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8623-5526"
repository-code: "https://github.com/berdakh/onset-hfo"
url: "https://berdakh.github.io/onset/"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - intracranial EEG
  - high-frequency oscillations
  - epilepsy
  - seizure onset zone
  - MNE-Python
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Interictal intracranial EEG with expert-validated HFO markings"
    authors:
      - name: "Fedele, T. et al."
    url: "https://openneuro.org/datasets/ds003498"
    notes: "The cohort every number in docs/EVALUATION.md was measured on."
